<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA1-010>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA1-010" ;
  triage:title "record_task_reminder collapses the durable write Result to a bare bool via .is_ok(), discarding the error cause without logging" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r1, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T12:38Z) at head da823baaa0018933f8daac388733c51eb14e9335. rust-best-practices-agent RBP-F001 and rust-qa-agent QA-002 (independently, same line): record_task_reminder (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:524) returns .is_ok() (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:537) on the durable write result, discarding the AtmError cause with no logging before returning false. Fix: propagate or log the error (warn with member/task/error) before mapping to the boolean outcome; consider returning Result to the caller. Crate-wide repeatable sweep for literal pattern .is_ok() in crates/atm-http-runtime found 10 additional textual matches (client.rs:1811,1815; http1_server.rs:390; lib.rs:861,863; peer_connection_pool.rs:433; peer_dial.rs:483,505,632; storage_and_nudge_router.rs:1950); all were inspected at head da823baaa0018933f8daac388733c51eb14e9335 and are test assertions or result-preserving branches (peer_connection_pool.rs:433 retains and returns the underlying Result) rather than instances of this defect shape, so no additional occurrences are recorded." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBP" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
